range bed level 0.15 0.35 rests at 0.35, back to 0.22 with stir, and lower still as the machine fills (stack)
range bed lfo>cut 0 0.6 the slow filter wobble (0.35 Hz), deeper with the orb's speed
range halo level 0 0.14 the bed's own partials an octave up: the mids that let the family carry on small speakers, in with stir
range sub level 0 0.25 synth_00006 at C1: the weight, growing with the number of motions
range root level 0 0.32 the root: wub_00001 lifted to C4, sines only (it throbs: a wub)
range third level 0 0.35 the third: synth_00005 lifted to E3, sines only
range fifth level 0 0.3 the fifth: synth_00003 lifted to G3, sines only
range seventh level 0 0.12 the seventh: a dark tone at Bb3
range cloud level 0 0.3 the chord, growing with the number of motions; spells raise it and pick the chord
range cloud gather 0.5 1 a soft cluster while searching, the chord once every ratio is an integer
range tide level 0 0.35 the near-miss flicker: the slow rising-falling loop, low-passed
bind stir bed level 0.35 0.22
bind stir halo level 0 0.14
bind stack bed level 0 -0.08 rel
bind stack sub level 0 0.25
bind orb.accel sub drive 0 0.08
bind orb.speed bed lfo>cut 0 0.6
bind tone.root root level 0 0.32
bind tone.third third level 0 0.35
bind tone.fifth fifth level 0 0.3
bind tone.seventh seventh level 0 0.12
bind tension seventh bank 0.2 0.8
bind stack cloud level 0 0.3
bind coherence cloud gather 0.5 1
bind radiance cloud reverb 0.5 0.9
bind fit root shimmer 0.3 0
bind fit third shimmer 0.3 0
bind orb.radius root cutoff 0.4 0.9
bind orb.radius halo cutoff 0.3 0.9
bind orb.radius third cutoff 0.35 0.9
bind orb.radius fifth cutoff 0.35 0.9
bind orb.radius seventh cutoff 0.2 0.7
bind orb.curl cloud drift 0.1 0.45
bind orb.curl fifth ph_pos 0 1
bind orb.speed root ph_pos 0 1
bind score tide level 0 0.35
note gravitic v1 (draft, 2026-09-26). Same plan as pyretic v3: bed at C2 (synth_00004), chord-tone voices at C4 / E3 / G3 / Bb3 brought in
note by tone.*, the cloud by stack and coherence. What is gravity here: a C1 sub that grows with stack (the more motions, the more mass),
note a slow filter wobble on the bed that deepens with the orb's speed, every voice's low-pass opened by the orb's radius, wide reverbs.
note One-shots: impact on lock, riser on accept, downer on unlock. The voices' residuals are off because these recordings are all sub.
note Names and recipes below are placeholders to rename; the recipes were checked buildable and non-degenerate.

